# Line endings, and one of these lines matters more here than it looks.
#
# `gradlew.bat` is broken on Windows if its CRLF are normalised away, which is what git announced it
# would do at the first commit. That is the ordinary reason for this file.
#
# **The goldens are the reason it is not ordinary.** This repository's design acceptance is a set of
# PNG bytes compared within a 0.05 % tolerance; a single byte rewritten by end-of-line normalisation
# is a diff nobody made, in the one artefact whose whole value is that a diff means something. Git
# detects binary content on its own and almost always gets it right — "almost always" is not the
# standard for the files a check compares byte for byte.
* text=auto

*.bat text eol=crlf
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.ttf binary
*.pbf binary
*.pmtiles binary
